    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d347-a1">

                <pb facs="0671" n="623" sameAs="frus:frus1877/pg623"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Chérif Pasha to Mr. Farman.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Ministry of Foreign Affairs</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Cairo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1877-02-12"><hi rendition="#italic">February</hi> 12,
                        1877</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Agent and Consul-General</hi>: By dispatch of the
                    10th of February, you did me the honor to inform me that the Hon. Secretary of
                    State at Washington asks whether any change has been made in the propositions
                    contained in my communication of the 3d of August, 1876, relative to the
                    augmentation of the number of judges of the new tribunals.</p>
                <p>I hasten to reply, Mr. Agent and Consul-General, that the necessities of the
                    judicial service remaining the same, the Government of the Khédive has not
                    changed its propositions, and that it is ready to carry them out, subject to the
                    conditions in my aforementioned communications of the, 3d of August, 1876, and
                    under the final reserves therein expressed.</p>
                <p>Be pleased, Mr. Agent and Consul-General, to accept the assurance of my high
                    consideration.</p>
                <closer><signed>CHÉRIF.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
